<div class="Story">
<div class="Story-section">
    <h4 class="Story-title">Base (LiveComponent — the payment step)</h4>
    <p class="Story-label">
        Lists the payment modules the shop offers for the cart of the session, so the list stands
        empty until there is one. Picking a module stores it on the cart and refreshes the step
        button.
    </p>
    <p class="Story-label">
        Under the modules come the consent boxes the shop asks for, in the order the merchant put
        them in, so this block is empty on a shop asking for none. A box carries its own live
        action rather than sitting in a form: the answer is kept by the server, which is both what
        the order is checked against and what gets frozen on it. A required box shows an asterisk
        and keeps the step button grey until it is ticked; the wording is printed as text, and the
        link to the full terms sits next to the box rather than inside its label, where clicking it
        would toggle the box. The long text the shop wrote, when there is one, is rendered under
        the box and tied to it for screen readers.
    </p>
    <div class="Story-stage Story-stage--roomy">
        <twig:Organisms:Payment:Base />
    </div>
</div>
</div>
